Both mutation probes were rejected with the expected symbolic residuals (`X+Y ≠ X+Y+1` and `X−Y ≠ X+Y`). Concrete LLVM execution also produced 5 and 12 for the prompt examples, and CPython matched an independent `operator.add` oracle on 49 integer pairs. I’ve put the complete reproducible sequence into `prove.sh` and am running it end-to-end once before writing the audit report.
exec
/bin/bash -lc 'chmod +x prove.sh && ./prove.sh > proof-run.log 2>&1; task_rc=$?; tail -n 120 proof-run.log; exit "$task_rc"' in /workspace
